  "north_star": "Trust is the single most important outcome of every video, because trust is what later lets the channel sell an e-book. Two absolute framing rules: (1) NEVER say out loud that the video is about trust or about building a relationship; it is shown, never announced; (2) NEVER address 'an audience' or 'you all'; speak to ONE person, directly, using Sie, as if teaching them and only them. Build trust three ways: deliver a genuinely valuable real teaching; show restraint by never forcing CTAs (credibility comes from NOT begging for likes, subscribes, or sign-ups); and position the material as rare, old, hard-to-find knowledge the viewer is fortunate to have found, which Matthias passes on from his own study. The character brand is itself a trust engine: a named, consistent person with a real biography and a life that visibly works. Every hook is a promise the script must keep. Import the buried-secret FORMAT and FRAMING; never import dishonest CONTENT.",

